cter's personality  before becoming an actor michael rooker  was a lifeguard for three years on a  beach in chicago but that kind of  experience didn't prepare rooker for  having to swim in his savant outfit and  wig it was interesting that physicality  was really the biggest kind of  physicality thing that was the most  challenging for me in this movie  john cena's peacemaker getup is  certainly goofy but not out of place in  james gunn's supervillain bonanza from  the silver toilet bowl like helmet he  wears to the tight red shirt one would  think that cena would be quite  uncomfortable in his super suit but over  the course of filming the suicide squad  as well as filming the peacemaker  spin-off series cena seemed to have  grown a fondness to his suit even  wearing it on talk shows to take naps  and he even wore it to the red carpet  i've learned that if you just keep the  costume on they don't ask for it back  the only downside to the suit according  to cena's co-star flula borg his cast  mates were constantly using his shiny  helmet to check their teeth um i am a  horrible superhero  joel kinnaman's rick flagg didn't fully  resemble his comic book counterpart in  the first film so when it came time for  the standalone sequel kinnaman and james  gunn wanted to make some changes  apparently it was kiniman himself who  really pushed hard for rick flagg to  wear the flashy yellow shirt and gun  suspenders which resemble the  character's attire in the dc comics  according to kineman james always wanted  to honor the original comic he really  owns that world it was a really good  plan too flulaborg was excited to  finally try out his javelin outfit but  the costume crew were extremely  secretive about it putting on the suit  was like an out of body experience for  borg i felt like i was walking around  with my shoulders back more and standing  taller i became an instant  because javelin is one american women  all love accents there was so much  effort put into makin